#
# STATUS: LIVE, 2026-11-15. A MEASUREMENT example for `win_vm.sh run --env-file FILE`, not a profile.
#
# Windows needs NO env file. Until 2026-11-14 this file held the 18 flags of the measured Windows profile
# (the recorded Code 0 holds, `traces/sweep_windows_20261021/p19.flags`); the gates that passed ran with
# all of them on (4 dies), and they are now the DEVICE'S DEFAULT for a guest that declares the measured Windows
# driver at fn 1 (`docs/design/V3_WINDOWS_SUPPORT_PROFILE.md`, `docs/OWNER_RULINGS.md` section AT, owner 2026-11-15:
# "set the measured Windows profile as the default"; the per-declaration form is not yet run on hardware). Setting any of those names does nothing now. The one opt-out is
# the device property `windows-support=off` (a Linux-only VM). The old file is in git history before this date.
#
# What an env file is for now: measurement flags that are off by default and change no behaviour, for example
# the RPC trace below (`win_vm.sh run` sets it anyway unless `--no-rpc-trace`). Only blank lines, '#' comments
# and KF3_NAME=digits lines are accepted; anything else refuses the file (win_vm.sh load_env_file). `run` logs
# the file's name, sha256 prefix and flag count (ENV_FILE) and the resulting KF3_* environment (KF3_ENV).
KF3_RPC_TRACE=1
